# Send these requests from VS Code (REST Client extension) or Visual Studio.
# Run them top to bottom. Replace {{loanId}} with the id returned by the first request.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@loanId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Create a loan
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applicantName": "Ayesha Khan",
  "accountNumber": "PK36SCBL0000001123456702",
  "amount": 250000,
  "tenureMonths": 12
}

### Get the loan
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/loans/{{loanId}}

### List approved loans (first page, newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/loans?status=Approved&pageSize=20

### Next page: paste the nextCursor value from the previous response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/loans?status=Approved&pageSize=20&cursor=PASTE_NEXT_CURSOR_HERE

### Approve
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/loans/{{loanId}}/approve

### Disburse
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/loans/{{loanId}}/disburse

### Disburse again: returns 409 Conflict, because the loan is already disbursed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/loans/{{loanId}}/disburse

### Reject (only works on a Pending loan)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/loans/{{loanId}}/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Insufficient income"
}
